{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The contested $6.00 is exactly the cancellation fee in force for an AIRPORT-zone no-show on this trip, and it reconciles with the fare breakdown's own derived money block: a zone-class fee of $6.00 against a charged cancellation line of $6.00, difference $0.00. There is therefore no fare integrity defect and POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged on the amount. The fare breakdown is COMPLETE at weight 1.0; the trip record is IMPAIRED at weight 0.4 with issue code CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT, which touches its arrival and dwell fields, not the charge amount.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00210", "EV-TRIP-00210"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.zone_class_fee",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trip record contains a driver 'arrived' event at 23:42:10 and shows the trip terminated by the driver at 23:49:05 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, which satisfies POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (d). The trip record is IMPAIRED at weight 0.4 with issue code CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT: those two fields are the platform's own telemetry, nothing else in the bundle contradicts the reason code, and the rider's own filing does not assert that he boarded or that the driver chose any other reason code.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00210"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.arrived_at",
      "asserted_weight": 0.4
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's trace contains 5 consecutive qualifying in-geofence fixes, more than the 3 consecutive in-radius fixes POL-NS-02 requires, with a minimum measured distance of 96.0 m from the pickup pin, inside the 150 m arrival radius that applies to the AIRPORT zone class. The trace is IMPAIRED at weight 0.25 with issue codes CLOCK_SKEW, GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW, LOW_COVERAGE, TRUNCATED_LOG, LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD; the clock defect shifts timestamps rather than positions, so the in-radius fix count is untouched by the discount and POL-NS-02's proximity test is met.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00210", "EV-TRIP-00210"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 0.25
    },
    {
      "text": "The record's own admissibility finding is that the driver device clock runs a known 228 s ahead of the server clock. Correcting the first qualifying in-geofence fix (device 23:42:21) by that known offset puts the driver inside the geofence at 23:38:33 server time, before the 23:42:10 arrived event, so POL-NS-01 limb (b) is met; and the continuous dwell from that fix to the 23:49:05 cancellation is 632 s, above the 480 s free waiting period in force for this AIRPORT trip, so limb (c) is met also. Read at face value the same span is only 404 s, which is why the correction matters - and the 186 s gap running from 23:39:15 to 23:42:21 sits exactly across geofence entry, so the export cannot be read at face value against the platform's own arrival event. The trace is IMPAIRED at weight 0.25 with issue codes CLOCK_SKEW, GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW, LOW_COVERAGE, TRUNCATED_LOG, LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD, and the trip record is IMPAIRED at weight 0.4 with CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00210", "EV-TRIP-00210"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.first_ts",
      "asserted_weight": 0.25
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-03 is not the governing clause. It applies only where the driver's stationary fixes lie outside the arrival radius but within 400 m of the pin, and it always ends in a full refund of the fee. Here the qualifying fixes lie inside the 150 m AIRPORT radius, the closest at 96.0 m, so the wrong-entrance regime is not engaged and does not displace the fee.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00210", "EV-TRIP-00210"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 0.25
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider. Limb (a) requires a rider message that is locating or coordinating and sent during the waiting window; the only rider message surviving in the log is sent at 23:49:40, thirty-five seconds after the driver's 23:49:05 cancellation, and the only in-window message is the SYSTEM notice 'Your driver has arrived' at 23:42:11, which is not the rider's own. Limb (c) cannot be run at all, because the trace carries no rider_track, so under POL-NS-11 it is undecidable and neutral and cannot exonerate. The chat log is IMPAIRED at weight 0.6 with issue code TRUNCATED_LOG - messages 002 and 003 implied by its own sequence numbering are missing - and I disclose that: the gap cuts both ways, and neither the surviving text nor the trip record's chat_message_count of 4 identifies any rider locating message inside the window.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00210", "EV-GPS-00210"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04", "POL-NS-11"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-05 cannot be run on this record. It requires matching the 'arrived' event to a GPS fix, and the record's own finding is that the 228 s clock skew makes any such matching unsafe under POL-NS-08(a), which must be applied before POL-NS-05 can operate. On the corrected clock the driver was inside the 150 m radius at the arrival marker, so neither limb of the false-arrival test - more than 300 m from the pin, or travelling at 15 km/h or above at that moment - is established. The trace is IMPAIRED at weight 0.25 with issue codes CLOCK_SKEW, GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW, LOW_COVERAGE, TRUNCATED_LOG, LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00210", "EV-TRIP-00210"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05", "POL-NS-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.25
    },
    {
      "text": "Where the fee stands, POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout at 80 percent of the $6.00 fee in force, which is $4.80, and the anti-farming check does not trip on either limb: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2, below the 4-termination limb, and 2 divided by completed_trips_30d of 156 is a rate of 0.013, far under the 0.08 limb. Those are exactly the two fields POL-NS-07 names, read as it names them.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00210", "EV-FARE-00210"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.driver_compensation",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even on the reading most hostile to the driver, the arrival and dwell facts rest solely on the GPS trace, and its impairment under POL-NS-08(a) (228 s clock skew) and POL-NS-08(b) (a 186 s gap inside the waiting window) takes the case at most to human review under POL-NS-09(e). Under POL-GEN-02(2) that single carrier caps confidence at 0.25, so it cannot alone support a ruling against the driver, and the disputed $6.00 is HELD rather than collected or refunded while review is pending. The driver's worst outcome on this record is a hold, not a refund to the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00210", "EV-FARE-00210"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.25
    }
  ]
}
